      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
